  "query_preview": "..\n(This afternoon through next Monday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: Skies are currently sunny across much of\nthew forecast area though some low to mid-level clouds can be seen\nover east-central and wester-central Nevada this afternoon.\nTemperatures continue to remain above normal for this time of\nyear. Look for quiet weather conditions tonight with lows in the\n30s.\n\nUpper level low pressure will be spinning out in the eastern\nPacific tomorrow. Moisture from the south will be pushing to the\nnorth. Favorable dynamics will help to promote isolated to\nscattered showers with the possibility of a few rumbles of\nthunder. Forecast surface-based CAPE values will be in the 100 to\nperhaps 150J/kg with weak instability mainly across central and \nportions of eastern Nevada Tuesday afternoon and evening. High \ntemperatures will be in the 60s and 70s with overnight lows in the\n30s and 40s.\n\nWednesday through Friday, the upper trough will gradually wobble\nits way towards western California on Wednesday. From here, models\nwill bring it ashore Wednesday, opening and crossing into \nsouthern and central Nevada by Thursday and Friday. Model trends\nhave been consistent in showing this to be a warm storm with snow\nlevels above 7500 feet. Rainfall amounts in the valleys over the\nWednesday through Friday timeframe have been increased and are\nfairly robust at a half-inch up to an inch. Highs during this\nperiod will be warm on Wednesday with readings in the 60s and 70s,\nbut cooling into the 50s and 60s by Thursday and Friday. Winds\nwill be breezy to locally windy each afternoon, especially in\ncentral Nevada where gusts to 35-40 mph are expected. Overnight\nlows will be in the 30s and 40s.\n\nThe upper system is expected to shift out of the forecast area for\nSaturday with dry conditions expected afterwards. Highs will be in\nthe 50s and 60s with lows in the 20s and 30s.\n\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: No changes were made to the NBM\nforecast through the short term. Confidence in the short term\nforecast remains high, though there are slight differences in the\ntiming and location of convective activity Tuesday and Wednesday.",
